From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] framework: a system notification's accent is black

Measured on V86 (2026-10-27) from a screenshot of the shade: the app name, the
secondary line and the action text of every system notification are grey 115
to 121, centred on 117. `system_notification_accent_color` is #ff607D8B (Blue
Grey 500), and its luma is 0.299*96 + 0.587*125 + 0.114*139 = 117.9. The panel
renders luma, so on this device that colour is grey 117; the measurement and
the arithmetic agree to within the text's antialiasing.

Rule 2 of docs/design/eink-ui.md: the accent is black, and a state is told
apart by shape and fill rather than by colour. Every system notification takes
its colour from this one entry, so one value settles all of them:
GlobalScreenshot.java:202 (the screenshot notice), PowerNotificationWarnings
.java:167, NotificationController.java:191 (print), BugreportProgressService
.java:1068, CarrierActionUtils.java:218 and GpsNetInitiatedHandler.java:395.

Only the value changes. Nothing is added, and nothing is written above the
entry: AOSP gives it no comment of its own and it keeps none, so
com.android.internal.R, framework.jar and the 45 ART boot files stay as they
are. Patch 0060's header records, with the hashes, what happens when a comment
is put above an entry in this file.

--- a/core/res/res/values/colors.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/values/colors.xml
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@
     <color name="accessibility_focus_highlight">#bf39b500</color>
     <color name="autofilled_highlight">#4dffeb3b</color>
 
-    <color name="system_notification_accent_color">#ff607D8B</color>
+    <color name="system_notification_accent_color">#ff000000</color>
 
     <!-- Default user icon colors -->
     <color name="user_icon_1">#ff00bcd4</color><!-- cyan 500 -->
